// Title: HackTool - Potential Remote Credential Dumping Activity Via CrackMapExec Or Impacket-Secretsdump
// Sigma ID: 6e2a900a-ced9-4e4a-a9c2-13e706f9518a
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: SecurityAura
// Date: 2022-11-16 | Modified: 2024-06-27
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1003
// Description: Detects default filenames output from the execution of CrackMapExec and Impacket-secretsdump
//   against an endpoint.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/Porchetta-Industries/CrackMapExec
//   - https://github.com/fortra/impacket/blob/ff8c200fd040b04d3b5ff05449646737f836235d/examples/secretsdump.py
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_hktl_remote_cred_dump.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\svchost.exe" and FolderPath matches regex "\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\[a-zA-Z0-9]{8}\\.tmp$"
